// Title: Suspicious Calculator Usage
// Sigma ID: 737e618a-a410-49b5-bec3-9e55ff7fbc15
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-02-09 | Modified: 2023-11-09
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036
// Description: Detects suspicious use of 'calc.exe' with command line parameters or in a suspicious directory,
//   which is likely caused by some PoC or detection evasion.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/ItsReallyNick/status/1094080242686312448
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_calc_uncommon_exec.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "\\calc.exe " or (FolderPath endswith "\\calc.exe" and (not((FolderPath contains ":\\Windows\\System32\\" or FolderPath contains ":\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\" or FolderPath contains ":\\Windows\\WinSxS\\"))))
